<title>GERMANY: WVZ details 2nd German sugar beet test data.</title>
<headline>WVZ details 2nd German sugar beet test data.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sugar industry association WVZ on Monday supplied the following details of the second German sugar beet test of the 1997/98 campaign, which showed a higher sugar yield and identical sugar content compared with 1996's second test.</p>
<p>Details --</p>
<p>			     2nd test 1997  1st test 1997  2nd test 1996</p>
<p> Sugar yield per ha     6.24 t	   3.93 t	   6.07 t</p>
<p> Sugar content (pct)    15.0 pct	12.6 pct	  15.0 pct</p>
<p> Sugar weight per root  75.0 grams    47.4 grams	71.8 grams</p>
<p> Avg root weight	  501 grams     376 grams	 477 grams</p>
<p> Avg no of beets/ha     83,200	  83,000	    84,600</p>
<p> Avg leaf weight	  666 grams     650 grams	 654 grams</p>
<p> Rain in past 2 wks	13 mm	   69 mm	     29 mm</p>
<p>NOTE -- The second 1997/98 test was taken on Friday, Aug 15 and results published on Aug 18. The first test this year was taken on Aug 1 and result was published on Aug 5.</p>
<p>The second test last year was taken on Aug 16, 1996 and results were published on Aug 19.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
